:name: IFS ECU (STM32H733) on a virtual MLC carrier
:description: Boots the ECU application image as the CAN bootloader would leave it, with each FDCAN on its own CAN hub.

using sysbus

$elf?=@/tmp/ECU08.elf

# A 500 us sync quantum (Renode default: 100 us) lets the ECU keep real-time
# pace on a desktop host: IFS_HIL's tests time the firmware with the wall
# clock. Still 20x finer than the firmware's fastest period (10 ms).
emulation SetGlobalQuantum "0.0005"

mach create "ecu"
machine LoadPlatformDescription $ORIGIN/../platforms/cpus/stm32h733.repl

# One hub per physical bus, so a test can attach to exactly the bus it means.
emulation CreateCANHub "can_inv"
emulation CreateCANHub "can_acu"
emulation CreateCANHub "can_dash"
connector Connect sysbus.fdcan1 can_inv
connector Connect sysbus.fdcan2 can_acu
connector Connect sysbus.fdcan3 can_dash

macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF $elf
    # The app is linked at 0x08020000 and never sets VTOR itself: the CAN
    # bootloader at 0x08000000 does that before jumping. Do the same here.
    cpu VectorTableOffset 0x08020000
"""

runMacro $reset

# The firmware polls ADC3 without setting PCSEL; Renode warns on every
# conversion (~300 lines/s), which is pure log overhead.
logLevel 3 sysbus.adc3
